237355dc8ba2a79cd970610f26a1915"}, "end_line": 289, "file_id": null, "generation": 1, "id": "documentsection:2036840a5ff662a2e81cc0e599e2170f0a357e4498e11548fa8cf6b79444491a", "kind": "DocumentSection", "language": "markdown", "metadata": {"anchor": "79c3f03a99dbabb5", "content_hash": "639fea05bcf31ff987fd2a0718a73b40717001f17435c6d00fab3a0f9a87e899", "document_id": "document:f9b8f4785a6ab6a6a8725bb6cac24c1953de4e699241e07aea735bc288df0f82", "document_type": "Document", "document_version": 279677322005281, "end_line": 289, "explicit_id": null, "heading_path": "���лᱻ���� / ���ؾ��� / c_murmurhash_bl", "layer": "knowledge", "path": "docs/cn/client.md", "start_line": 286, "text": "### c_murmurhash_bl\n\n�����������޵�һ���Թ�ϣ��\"Consistent Hashing with Bounded Loads\"��Mirrokni�ȣ�CACM 2017������ϣ����`c_murmurhash`��ȫ��ͬ����ÿ̨��������������������`ceil(load_factor * ƽ����;������)`������ϣ���еķ������Ѵ�����ʱ�������ع�ϣ��˳ʱ���������һ̨�������ķ�����������ȵ�key����ѹ�嵥̨����������������������䵽���Ϲ̶��ĺ�̽ڵ㣬��cache��Ȼ�Ѻá�ϵ��Ĭ������-chash_bounded_load_factor��Ĭ��1.25���������1�����ɰ�channel���ǣ�`c_murmurhash_bl:load_factor=1.5`��`replicas`������`c_murmurhash`��ͬ��\n", "title": "c_murmurhash_bl"}, "name": "c_murmurhash_bl", "qualified_name": "docs/cn/client.md#79c3f03a99dbabb5", "relation": "DOCUMENTS", "repo_id": "repo:074b46c6e95703171fcd66ba04121d7fcacc04ef0fa2e0085f37e49cc4137eac", "shard_id": null, "signature": null, "source_hash": "639fea05bcf31ff987fd2a0718a73b40717001f17435c6d00fab3a0f9a87e899", "start_line": 286}, {"edge_metadata": {"document_path": "docs/en/client.md", "layer": "knowledge", "raw_evidence_link_id": "evidence:0c8d3c537a44fa979b86bf3a68d7464b5bf44b5d20a746176c702b9071a3ee0b"}, "end_line": 290, "file_id": null, "generation": 1, "id": "documentsection:4a4e65b39c3cd0e885b6a187eba68573f1e3db083fe725bb19d6c5bcf4af453c", "kind": "DocumentSection", "language": "markdown", "metadata": {"anchor": "10b2646294acf078", "content_hash": "0829f12ca808ae3f8d71fd69ce3e2b22f247d9e3643b7299a0e1216910c6d027", "document_id": "document:eba0523fcecc3112b53e246d80313bbc85cc61d5bf266c7d451e69b2b26758d3", "document_type": "Document", "document_version": 265997620039643, "end_line": 290, "explicit_id": null, "heading_path": "This line is ignored / Load Balancer / c_murmurhash_bl", "layer": "knowledge", "path": "docs/en/client.md", "start_line": 287, "text": "### c_murmurhash_bl\n\nwhich is consistent hashing with bounded loads(\"Consistent Hashing with Bounded Loads\", Mirrokni et al., CACM 2017). The hash ring is identical to `c_murmurhash`, but each server additionally has a capacity of `ceil(load_factor * average in-flight requests)`. When the hashed-to server is at capacity, the request overflows clockwise to the next server on the ring with spare capacity, so a hot key no longer saturates a single server while overflowed requests always land on the same ring successors, which keeps caches effective. The default factor comes from -chash_bounded_load_factor(default 1.25, must be > 1) and can be overridden per channel: `c_murmurhash_bl:load_factor=1.5`. The `replicas` parameter is supported as in `c_murmurhash`.\n", "title": "c_murmurhash_bl"}, "name": "c_murmurhash_bl", "qualified_name": "docs/en/client.md#10b2646294acf078", "relation": "DOCUMENTS", "repo_id": "repo:074b46c6e95703171fcd66ba04121d7fcacc04ef0fa2e0085f37e49cc4137eac", "shard_id": null, "signature": null, "source_hash": "0829f12ca808ae3f8d71fd69ce3e2b22f247d9e3643b7299a0e1216910c6d027", "start_line": 287}], "returned_evidence_count": 4, "returned_evidence_ids": ["E-XLINK-3284c4dde04ede3b45992a17", "E-XLINK-e0e9be2cf50f895bf973243a", "E-CODE-9cec5b84fb52b556c0c332c9", "E-SHARD-6487ab8c99b36b477f261e90"], "summary": "Function brpc.policy.AddServersInBatch.replicas ()", "supporting_evidence": [{"commit": "ae09e960c7291605dda52356cc0c2d45567fb53e", "confidence": 1.0, "evidence_id": "E-CODE-9cec5b84fb52b556c0c332c9", "generation": 1, "kind": "CODE_DEFINITION", "metadata": {"bundle_profile": 